<body>
  <%- include('./partials/nav') %>
  <div class="container-fluid p-3 info-container">

    <div class="intro">
      <h1 class="text-center">Fast Virtual Tabletop for Online RPGs</h1>
      <p>
        Start a live table in minutes, then run full sessions with tactical tools that hold up in real play.
        Far Reach Co gives you fast invite-link setup plus layers, grid controls, drawing, token management,
        chat dice rolling, and map-to-map links via location pins in one VTT workflow.
      </p>
      <hr>
    </div>

    <!-- 1. Fast Setup -->
    <section id="fast-setup">
      <h2>Fast Setup: From Link to Live Table in Minutes</h2>
      <p>
        Setup speed matters when a session is about to start. Use the no-signup sandbox for instant trials,
        or create a full table and share one link with your group.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Launch quickly</strong> - start a guest sandbox or full table in a few clicks.</li>
        <li><strong>Share one join link</strong> - players can enter without account friction.</li>
        <li><strong>Pick your mode</strong> - use Standard for full tools or Sandbox for focused rehearsal.</li>
        <li><strong>Stay in session flow</strong> - less setup overhead before the first encounter.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 2. Core Features -->
    <section id="core-features">
      <h2>Core Virtual Tabletop Features for Live Play</h2>
      <p>
        The toolset is built for active encounters, not just map display.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Token controls</strong> - move, resize, rotate, lock/unlock, and manage visibility.</li>
        <li><strong>Map/Object/Fog layers</strong> - separate terrain, interactive pieces, and fog effects.</li>
        <li><strong>Grid controls</strong> - show/hide grid, resize dimensions, and use snap movement.</li>
        <li><strong>Drawing tools</strong> - freehand, lines, shapes, and text for live annotations.</li>
        <li><strong>Chat + dice</strong> - table chat and <code>/roll</code> commands in the same workspace.</li>
        <li><strong>Location pins</strong> - mark key map locations and link tables for smooth scene transitions.</li>
        <li><strong>Image folders</strong> - organize maps and tokens for faster scene changes.</li>
        <li><strong>Template system</strong> - save and load table setups for repeatable encounters.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. GM Session Control -->
    <section id="gm-control">
      <h2>GM Control Without Slowing the Session</h2>
      <p>
        Keep encounters moving while preserving control over table state and player view.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Object visibility controls</strong> - hide or reveal pieces as scenes evolve.</li>
        <li><strong>Layer and ordering tools</strong> - keep tactical information readable during combat.</li>
        <li><strong>Pin management</strong> - locate, restore, or clean up map markers quickly.</li>
        <li><strong>Role-aware permissions</strong> - managers keep full controls while participants interact in real time.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 4. Campaign Depth -->
    <section id="campaign-depth">
      <h2>Scale from One-Shots to Persistent Campaigns</h2>
      <p>
        When a group becomes long-term, move into Wyrlds so campaign state stays organized between sessions.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Linked multi-map play</strong> - connect rooms, regions, and encounter maps with location pins.</li>
        <li><strong>Persistent records</strong> - keep lore, NPC notes, and session history in one campaign hub.</li>
        <li><strong>Character support</strong> - attach D&amp;D 5E character sheets to your campaign flow.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 5. Competitive Search Intent -->
    <section id="alternatives">
      <h2>Need an Alternative to Roll20 or Owlbear Rodeo?</h2>
      <p>
        Far Reach Co is built for groups that want fast startup without giving up core tabletop features.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Fast onboarding</strong> - invite-link joining and no-signup sandbox testing.</li>
        <li><strong>Feature-complete sessions</strong> - layers, fog, grid, drawing, chat/dice, and location pins.</li>
        <li><strong>Campaign continuity</strong> - persistent Wyrlds when your one-shot grows into a full arc.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section id="get-started">
      <div class="seo-cta-block">
        <p>Ready to run your first session? It takes less than two minutes to set up.</p>
        <a class="seo-cta-primary" href="/vtt/guest/start">Try the VTT Free - No Signup</a>
        <a class="seo-cta-secondary" href="/register">Create a Free Account</a>
        <a class="seo-cta-secondary" href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLbXvAcAjBp22C6lKdWlSd32I_6US4O2wa" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch Existing VTT Tutorials</a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
  <%- include('./partials/footer') %>
</body>

